# Example: /etc/crypttab (for reference only)
#
# This file is normally already created by your OS installer when you set up
# LUKS encryption — this guide does not create or modify it. It's included
# here only so the volume name referenced elsewhere (dm_crypt-0, in this
# guide's tested example) makes sense in context.
#
# Format: <target-name> <source-device-or-UUID> <key-file> <options>

# dm_crypt-0 UUID=<YOUR-LUKS-UUID> none luks,discard

# Find your own device's UUID with:
#   sudo blkid
